WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.134 line:92%
-I'm so happy to have you here.

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:02.669 align:start size:94% position:6%
We were talking backstage
about how you've been

00:00:02.669 --> 00:00:03.503 line:92%
a New Yorker your whole life.

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:06.606
But not only are you near,
you're very comfortable here,

00:00:06.606 --> 00:00:10.744 align:start size:94% position:6%
because your father
used to work in Studio 8H.

00:00:10.744 --> 00:00:11.578 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes, he did.

00:00:11.578 --> 00:00:13.880 line:92%
My dad was a bass violinist with

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:17.250 align:start size:94% position:6%
Arturo Toscanini
and the NBC Symphony.

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:20.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we used to watch
the rehearsals.

00:00:20.153 --> 00:00:22.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oh, thank you.
-Yes. Very wonderful.

00:00:22.389 --> 00:00:23.123 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:23.123 --> 00:00:26.726 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And it gave me
a lot of connections,

00:00:26.726 --> 00:00:30.063 align:start size:94% position:6%
because he was a staff --
He also was in

00:00:30.063 --> 00:00:32.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
the original band
of "The Tonight Show,"

00:00:32.532 --> 00:00:33.400 line:92%
the Steve Allen "Tonight Show."

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:37.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's incredible.
-Skitch Henderson conducting.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:41.307 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, I got on to
"The Howdy Doody Show."

00:00:41.307 --> 00:00:42.108 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Wow!

00:00:42.108 --> 00:00:44.644
Now this -- For those --
You were not in this photo,

00:00:44.644 --> 00:00:46.446
but this is what you were
doing on the "Howdy --"

00:00:46.446 --> 00:00:47.614 line:92%
You were one of the children.

00:00:47.614 --> 00:00:50.250 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Howdy Doody"
had a peanut gallery.

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:52.118 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, we didn't have
a lot of choices

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:54.554 size:84% position:42% line:92%
in those days of shows.

00:00:54.554 --> 00:00:57.323 line:92%
And I remember the theme song.

00:00:57.323 --> 00:00:59.359 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You do?
-Yeah. Ready?

00:00:59.359 --> 00:00:59.993 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:00:59.993 --> 00:01:02.662 line:92%
-♪♪ It's Howdy Doody time ♪♪

00:01:02.662 --> 00:01:04.431 line:92%
♪♪ It's Howdy Doody time ♪♪

00:01:04.431 --> 00:01:06.299 line:92%
♪♪ Bob Smith and Howdy Do ♪♪

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:07.901 line:92%
♪♪ Say howdy do to you ♪♪

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:09.602 line:92%
♪♪ Let's give a rousing cheer ♪♪

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:11.204 line:92%
♪♪ 'Cause Howdy Doody's here ♪♪

00:01:11.204 --> 00:01:12.906 line:92%
♪♪ It's time to start the show ♪♪

00:01:12.906 --> 00:01:14.541 size:88% position:44% line:92%
♪♪ So, kids, let's go ♪♪

00:01:14.541 --> 00:01:19.712 size:84% position:42%
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Oh, that's wonderful.

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:22.749 size:78% position:39% line:92%
I mean, I want to say

00:01:22.749 --> 00:01:24.884 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm impressed you
remembered the lyrics,

00:01:24.884 --> 00:01:27.087 align:start size:94% position:6%
but like half of it
is just his name.

00:01:27.087 --> 00:01:29.255 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was a lot of
Howdy Doody in that.

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:31.624 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And, you know,
Clarabell the Clown...

00:01:31.624 --> 00:01:32.092 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes?

00:01:32.092 --> 00:01:33.893
-...who actually --
They would run a little contest.

00:01:33.893 --> 00:01:36.596
I got picked, naturally,
'cause I had connections.

00:01:36.596 --> 00:01:38.098 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, of course.

00:01:38.098 --> 00:01:41.334 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And Clarabell became
Captain Kangaroo.

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:42.669 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, wow.
-Bob Keeshan. Yeah.

00:01:42.669 --> 00:01:46.372
And then there was Princess
Summerfall Winterspring.

00:01:46.372 --> 00:01:46.840 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Uh-huh.

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:48.274 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And there was
a big scandal about her.

00:01:48.274 --> 00:01:51.811
I have to go Google it now that
my memory isn't that good.

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:52.712 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Right.

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:53.746 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-But, yeah, it was --

00:01:53.746 --> 00:01:57.383
-I can't believe you're just
going to leave us with that.

00:01:57.383 --> 00:01:57.817 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I know.

00:01:57.817 --> 00:02:01.287 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think everyone
should go Google that.

00:02:01.287 --> 00:02:03.123 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Princess
Summerfall Winterspring.

00:02:03.123 --> 00:02:04.724
-Oh, yeah.
She killed someone with her car.

00:02:04.724 --> 00:02:09.362 align:start size:94% position:6%
That was it. I'm just kidding.
I don't know.

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:12.165 align:start size:94% position:6%
You -- People don't know
this about you.

00:02:12.165 --> 00:02:14.634
You know, I think there's
a generation that knows you

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:17.003 align:start size:94% position:6%
fully as this wonderful
comedic actress,

00:02:17.003 --> 00:02:19.506 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you began doing
dramatic roles.

00:02:19.506 --> 00:02:22.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
You were in a Clint Eastwood
thriller called

00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:23.810 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Play Misty for Me"
and other films.

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:25.678 size:84% position:42%
Did it take a long time
for people to see you

00:02:25.678 --> 00:02:27.447 size:78% position:39%
as somebody who could
do comedy, as well?

00:02:27.447 --> 00:02:31.885
-You know, I couldn't get a
sitcom until I was 40 years old.

00:02:31.885 --> 00:02:32.752 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow.
-This is true.

00:02:32.752 --> 00:02:37.557 align:start size:94% position:6%
Ellen Travolta played the mom
on "Joanie Loves Chachi."

00:02:37.557 --> 00:02:38.224 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Mm-hmm.

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:39.225 line:92%
-And there was a story line --

00:02:39.225 --> 00:02:42.495 align:start size:94% position:6%
We had done a show in
summer stock, she and I.

00:02:42.495 --> 00:02:43.463 line:92%
There was a story line about --

00:02:43.463 --> 00:02:46.266
She was, you know, the mom
that stayed home with the kids,

00:02:46.266 --> 00:02:47.467 align:start size:94% position:6%
and she had this
friend from high school

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:52.972 align:start size:94% position:6%
who was the career-driven
businesswoman, snotty, nasty,

00:02:52.972 --> 00:02:54.741 align:start size:94% position:6%
so, naturally,
she thought of me.

00:02:54.741 --> 00:03:00.046 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she suggested me for
the part, and I got the part.

00:03:00.046 --> 00:03:01.748 line:92%
And Garry Marshall produced it.

00:03:01.748 --> 00:03:03.249 align:start size:94% position:6%
And from then,
I got "Flamingo Kid,"

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:08.188 align:start size:94% position:6%
and a whole world
opened up in that area.

00:03:08.188 --> 00:03:09.689 align:start size:94% position:6%
You did a -- Didn't you do
a movie with Garry?

00:03:09.689 --> 00:03:11.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I did do a movie
with Garry Marshall.

00:03:11.291 --> 00:03:13.426 align:start size:94% position:6%
He was one of the
greatest guys of all time.

00:03:13.426 --> 00:03:14.994 line:92%
Just the sweetest, sweetest man.

00:03:14.994 --> 00:03:17.330 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is Garry Marshall
directing.

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:18.231 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Okay.

00:03:18.231 --> 00:03:20.633 line:92%
-"You know, you'll stand there.

00:03:20.633 --> 00:03:23.403 align:start size:94% position:6%
You'll think of something.
You'll be funny."

00:03:23.403 --> 00:03:24.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he walks away.
-Yeah.

00:03:24.771 --> 00:03:28.908 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Am I right?
-Yeah, yeah.

00:03:28.908 --> 00:03:30.910 size:78% position:39%
You -- I want to ask,
because, obviously,

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:33.346 align:start size:94% position:6%
you do a lot of drinking
on the show.

00:03:33.346 --> 00:03:35.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
-On the show.
-Yeah, on the show.

00:03:35.114 --> 00:03:37.250 align:start size:94% position:6%
What are you actually drinking
on "Arrested Development"?

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:41.287 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, you know,
if we really drank the drinks,

00:03:41.287 --> 00:03:43.489 line:92%
we wouldn't be able to walk.

00:03:43.489 --> 00:03:46.025 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, you know,
for Martinis, it's water.

00:03:46.025 --> 00:03:46.926 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-With an Olive.

00:03:46.926 --> 00:03:51.831 align:start size:94% position:6%
And for white wine,
it's apple juice.

00:03:51.831 --> 00:03:56.703
Red wine is grape juice.
It's, you know, boring, boring.

00:03:56.703 --> 00:04:01.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, in real life, I do enjoy,
occasionally, a Martini,

00:04:01.441 --> 00:04:02.909 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I know how to
make a great one.

00:04:02.909 --> 00:04:03.743 line:92%
-Oh, wow. Well, there you go.

00:04:03.743 --> 00:04:05.612 size:84% position:42%
Next time you're here,
you'll have to show me.

00:04:05.612 --> 00:04:08.081
But there's something else
I want to ask you to show me.

00:04:08.081 --> 00:04:12.051 align:start size:94% position:6%
The Lucille wink.
Is this a teachable skill?

00:04:12.051 --> 00:04:12.685 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, my God.

00:04:12.685 --> 00:04:14.187 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Can you teach me
how to do it or is it --

00:04:14.187 --> 00:04:14.721 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-All right.

00:04:14.721 --> 00:04:16.723 align:start size:94% position:6%
For those -- I don't know
if everybody knows

00:04:16.723 --> 00:04:20.593 line:92%
the Lucille wink, but it's this.

00:04:20.593 --> 00:04:25.298
And the thing is -- one eye
has to completely close.

00:04:25.298 --> 00:04:28.201 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. Okay.
-This is not easy.

00:04:28.201 --> 00:04:28.801 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Gotcha. Okay.

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:31.170
-It's like, you know,
people that are double-jointed.

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:33.673 align:start size:94% position:6%
Either you can do it
or you can't.

00:04:33.673 --> 00:04:35.375 align:start size:94% position:6%
But you could try.
-Okay.

00:04:35.375 --> 00:04:38.911 line:92%
-So, let's see if you can do it.

00:04:38.911 --> 00:04:39.779 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
No.

00:04:39.779 --> 00:04:42.515 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No?
-No.

00:04:42.515 --> 00:04:43.883 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No.
-No. Okay.

00:04:43.883 --> 00:04:46.185 align:start size:94% position:6%
You didn't seem on the fence
about that at all.

00:04:46.185 --> 00:04:47.720 line:92%
That was a really hard "no."

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:49.756 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, it's...

00:04:49.756 --> 00:04:51.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, I don't think
I can do it, yeah.

00:04:51.291 --> 00:04:55.328 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, it's funny, because
I did it once on the set,

00:04:55.328 --> 00:04:57.764 align:start size:94% position:6%
and -- I don't know --
they liked it.

00:04:57.764 --> 00:04:58.598 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:04:58.598 --> 00:05:00.566 line:92%
-So, you know, they said,

00:05:00.566 --> 00:05:01.801 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You know, let's do it
whenever we can."

00:05:01.801 --> 00:05:05.238
-That's a wonder-- I mean, it's
one of the wonderful things

00:05:05.238 --> 00:05:07.340 align:start size:94% position:6%
about that show is it seemed
like it always found

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:10.143
things that people were good at
that not only you guys liked,

00:05:10.143 --> 00:05:12.378 size:84% position:42%
but the audience liked,
and then it made sure

00:05:12.378 --> 00:05:13.713 line:92%
to constantly reward us with it.

00:05:13.713 --> 00:05:17.317
-The writing on that show --
Well, as you, a great writer --

00:05:17.317 --> 00:05:21.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's the best, yeah.
-That writing -- so specific.

00:05:21.254 --> 00:05:22.388 line:92%
The characters were so --

00:05:22.388 --> 00:05:24.557 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And plots and everything
tying together.

00:05:24.557 --> 00:05:29.629 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you have a -- Your role on
"Archer" was also --

00:05:29.629 --> 00:05:32.398
Malory was also based on Lucille
a little bit, you were told.

00:05:32.398 --> 00:05:38.137
-Well, you know, the thing about
that was that I got copy.

00:05:38.137 --> 00:05:41.607 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, an agent sends you
copy for an audition.

00:05:41.607 --> 00:05:43.643 align:start size:94% position:6%
And one agent --
I have two agents.

00:05:43.643 --> 00:05:45.078 align:start size:94% position:6%
One is --
They're all different now,

00:05:45.078 --> 00:05:48.281 align:start size:94% position:6%
but, back then,
one was a commercial agent,

00:05:48.281 --> 00:05:49.515 line:92%
and one was a theatrical.

00:05:49.515 --> 00:05:51.217 line:92%
And the first copy I got was --

00:05:51.217 --> 00:05:53.252 align:start size:94% position:6%
It said, you know,
just "here's the part."

00:05:53.252 --> 00:05:59.792
The second copy said, "Malory --
think Jessica Walter

00:05:59.792 --> 00:06:02.362 line:92%
from 'Arrested Development.'"

00:06:02.362 --> 00:06:04.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I called the agent
and I said,

00:06:04.364 --> 00:06:08.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Well, you know, why don't you
send me the script.

00:06:08.167 --> 00:06:09.769 size:78% position:39% line:92%
I like it, you know?"

00:06:09.769 --> 00:06:10.603 line:92%
And that's how it came about.

00:06:10.603 --> 00:06:14.073 size:84% position:42%
But why would one agent
take my name out of it?

00:06:14.073 --> 00:06:14.907 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:06:14.907 --> 00:06:15.775 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Ooh!
-Ooh!

00:06:15.775 --> 00:06:18.745 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, I'm just glad you didn't
have that awkward moment

00:06:18.745 --> 00:06:20.646 size:78% position:39%
where you auditioned,
and they were like,

00:06:20.646 --> 00:06:23.649 line:92%
"No, not that Jessica Walter."

00:06:23.649 --> 00:06:25.852
It worked out.
-I've had those. I've had those.

00:06:25.852 --> 00:06:28.554 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, we all have had those.
-Yeah, voice-overs.

00:06:28.554 --> 00:06:29.756 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hey, thank you so much
for being here.

00:06:29.756 --> 00:06:32.625 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's such a pleasure
to meet you.

